ed the crowd with music.","tr":"Kalabalığı müzikle keyiflendirdiler."}]}],"variants":[],"phonetic":"/ˈdʒɒli/","band":1},{"id":"gen-b3-jolt","headword":"jolt","cefr":"C1","sourceCollection":"extended","sourceOrder":4941,"sourceEntry":"jolt n., v.","senses":[{"id":"gen-b3-jolt-n","partOfSpeech":"n.","turkishMeanings":["sarsıntı","sarsıcı darbe","şok"],"examples":[{"en":"The bus gave a jolt.","tr":"Otobüs bir sarsıntı yaptı."},{"en":"The news was a jolt.","tr":"Haber bir şoktu."},{"en":"He felt a jolt of pain.","tr":"Bir ağrı sarsıntısı hissetti."}]},{"id":"gen-b3-jolt-v","partOfSpeech":"v.","turkishMeanings":["sarsmak","sarsılmak","şok etmek"],"examples":[{"en":"The cart jolted over the stones.","tr":"Araba taşların üstünde sarsıldı."},{"en":"The news jolted them awake.","tr":"Haber onları sarsarak uyandırdı."},{"en":"The train jolted to a stop.","tr":"Tren sarsılarak durdu."}]}],"variants":[],"phonetic":"/dʒəʊlt/","band":3},{"id":"gen-b2-joss","headword":"joss","cefr":"C1","sourceCollection":"extended","sourceOrder":3282,"sourceEntry":"joss n.","senses":[{"id":"gen-b2-joss-n","partOfSpeech":"n.","turkishMeanings":["Çin tapınak putu","şans"],"examples":[{"en":"A joss stood in the temple.","tr":"Tapınakta bir put duruyordu."},{"en":"They burned joss sticks.","tr":"Tütsü çubukları yaktılar."},{"en":"The old joss was carved from wood.","tr":"Eski put ahşaptan oyulmuştu."}]}],"variants":[],"phonetic":"/dʒɒs/","band":2},{"id":"gen-b2-joyful","headword":"joyful","cefr":"C1","sourceCollection":"extended","sourceOrder":2319,"sourceEntry":"joyful adj.","senses":[{"id":"gen-b2-joyful-adj","partOfSpeech":"adj.","turkishMeanings":["neşeli","sevinçli","mutlu"],"examples":[{"en":"It was a joyful reunion.","tr":"Sevinçli bir kavuşmaydı."},{"en":"She gave a joyful cry.","tr":"Neşeli bir çığlık attı."},{"en":"The music sounded joyful.","tr":"Müzik neşeli geliyordu."}]}],"variants":[],"phonetic":"/ˈdʒɔɪfəl/","band":2},{"id":"gen-b2-joyous","headword":"joyous","cefr":"C1","sourceCollect